{
  "title": "test_failed_reasks_keep_the_answer_and_are_retryable times out when the suite runs slowly",
  "description": "tests/test_ingredient_names.py::test_failed_reasks_keep_the_answer_and_are_retryable waits up to 60s (line ~205) for the failed re-ask to show in /api/ingredient-names/status failures. \
On 2026-10-03 one local make test run took 80s instead of the usual ~25s and this wait timed out; an immediate rerun passed. \
The worker is shared with every other test that queues names, so under load the flagged row may wait behind pending batches (work_pass alternates pending and reasked batches). \
Find what the worker was doing during the wait (server logs in logs/test.log) and make the test independent of queue depth, e.g. by resolving only this name, rather than raising the timeout.",
